# Everything Hearth writes into whichever project is open. That set of folders
# includes the example games in this repo the moment anyone opens one, so each
# rule here has to match INSIDE packages/examples/* as well as at the root.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing, and is the whole reason this block is worth a comment.
# A pattern with an interior slash is anchored to its own .gitignore's
# directory, so a bare `.hearth/evidence/` matches only `<repo>/.hearth/`, which
# nothing ever writes — it silently protected nothing while reading as though it
# protected the example projects. Every rule below is per-project, so every rule
# below carries the prefix. See tests/gitignoreCoverage.test.ts, which fails if
# one loses it.
#
# Playtest output — sweeps and their evidence (journals, captures, results) are
# runtime artifacts, never sources.
**/.hearth/evidence/
**/.hearth/sweeps/
# Conversations and tester sessions are the user's own record of working in a
# folder, and a transcript of someone's afternoon is not a source file.
**/.hearth/chats/
**/.hearth/tester/
# The agent's command journal: runtime, and regenerated.
**/.hearth/log/
# API keys. The app drops a `.hearth/.gitignore` beside this file the first time
# settings are saved, but that guard is written on save and this repo has to
# hold whether or not anyone has saved yet.
**/.hearth/app.json

# agent/automation scratch (never commit to the public repo)
.scratch-audit/
.hearth-tmp/
scratch/
# Internal SDD/agent workflow artifacts. /.superpowers/, /.claude/, and
# /.worktrees/ are anchored to the repo root only, so example projects' own
# .claude/skills scaffolding stays tracked.
#
# The superpowers pattern needs the leading **/ and it is not decoration: a
# gitignore pattern with a slash anywhere but the end is ANCHORED to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so a bare `docs/superpowers/` matches only
# the copy at the repo root. It was written that way on purpose to catch nested
# copies and silently did not — `apps/editor/docs/superpowers/` held seven
# internal specs and plans, untracked and unignored, one `git add -A` away from
# a public repo. Check with `git check-ignore -v <path>`, never by reading it.
/.superpowers/
**/docs/superpowers/
/.claude/
/.worktrees/

# The Supabase CLI drops this wherever it is run; the catalog's project lives
# in its own repo and nothing here needs it.
**/supabase/.temp/
